  "id": "coldwatersentinel",
  "neon": "#5fd0ff",
  "note": "The city paper, mid-basin — the transition band, so it is modern but not glass: a stepped block with one cantilevered floor, a centred chamfered clock stage and a drum lantern with a mast. The restraint is the gradient doing its job. West of here the towers twist; east of here they are boxes; this is the middle and should look like somebody rebuilt the top two floors in 2070 and left the rest alone. ⚠ A CANTILEVER AND A ROTATION NEVER SHARE A SEGMENT — see the warning in aurelia.json. An offset box and a yawed box are each safe; a box that is both puts the derived kit where its own solid is not, and glself catches it. So asymmetry here is offset-only and every chamfer is CENTRED. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the sentinel arm back.",
